// ── ziggfreed-common's UI tokens: every colour and named size the kit draws with ──
// Imported per document as:  $ZK = "../Common/ZigTokens.ui";  (from Pages/; "ZigTokens.ui" from Common/) and
// used as  TextColor: $ZK.@ZigInkBody  or  Anchor: (Height: $ZK.@ZigRowHeight);  a named value reads across
// documents the way vanilla reads $C.@ColorDefaultLabel and $C.@SmallButtonHeight.
//
// No other kit document spells a colour: a colour changes here, once, for every row, tile, pill and page built on
// the kit. com.ziggfreed.common.ui.kit.ZigTokens holds the same names and values for the few colours Java pushes
// (a tone's fill on an accent bar, a dot's tint), and the kit's document tests hold the two together; its contrast
// test measures every ink and tone here against every surface laid over the band body.
//
// The palette is the game's Chapter screen (its design system's slate inks, gold marks, copper tagline and warm
// selection), drawn over the game's own modal band (Common/BackgroundModal.png).
//
// This document imports nothing: it is where every value starts.

// Inks: text colours, brightest first. Faint is the darkest player text allowed at the 13 floor; dim reads only
// at 20 and up (the large-text floor).
@ZigInkBright = #ffffff;
@ZigInkStrong = #d1dae6;
@ZigInkBody = #98a2b1;
@ZigInkMuted = #7a8aa0;
@ZigInkFaint = #79899f;
@ZigInkDim = #6e7a8c;
@ZigInkSection = #b4c8c9;
@ZigInkHeading = #b4c8c9;
// The tagline's copper, under a title.
@ZigInkCopper = #c58643;

// Surfaces: vanilla's pane, a list row in three states and its warm selected row, the scrim under a pill, no fill
// at all, vanilla's simple button fill (@ZigSurfaceTab: kept for a document that reads it; no kit document or painter
// draws it now that the rail's tabs take the row's hover and its warm selected row), the rule, the band body every
// surface is judged over (the modal band's own colour), and the scrim the band frames lay over the blurred world,
// which with a page's own overlay (Common.ui @PageOverlay, 0.45) darkens it as the game's modal does
// (Common/IntroModal.ui, 0.70).
@ZigSurfacePane = #000000(0.15);
@ZigSurfaceRow = #172230(0.85);
@ZigSurfaceRowHover = #12203f(0.92);
@ZigSurfaceRowPressed = #101a28(0.92);
@ZigSurfaceRowSelected = #3b2e21(0.92);
@ZigSurfaceScrim = #0a1119(0.8);
@ZigSurfaceClear = #000000(0);
@ZigSurfaceTab = #000000(0.2);
@ZigDivider = #48455c(0.6);
@ZigBandBody = #161e32;
@ZigBandScrim = #000000(0.45);
// Gold: points and Collect.
@ZigAccent = #e8a93b;
// Marks: a lit mark and a title in flat gold (the gold gradient's darkest stop, Common/TextGradient.png, so a flat
// title matches a masked one), and an unlit mark.
@ZigMarkLit = #e8b962;
@ZigMarkUnlit = #4a566b;

// Tones: a meaning's fill (an accent bar, a dot, a pill) and its text (a state word). Tones are semantic, so a
// theme never changes them: done reads green in every theme.
@ZigToneActiveFill = #4274a5;
@ZigToneActiveText = #7a9cc6;
@ZigToneCollectFill = #e8a93b;
@ZigToneCollectText = #e8a93b;
@ZigToneDoneFill = #4f9e63;
@ZigToneDoneText = #7fc893;
@ZigToneLiveFill = #4f9e63;
@ZigToneLiveText = #7fc893;
@ZigToneAvailableFill = #c08a3a;
@ZigToneAvailableText = #d9a75e;
@ZigToneWaitingFill = #7a64a0;
@ZigToneWaitingText = #b3a0d1;
@ZigToneBlockedFill = #5c6e80;
@ZigToneBlockedText = #96a9be;
@ZigToneDangerFill = #b04a4a;
@ZigToneDangerText = #e08080;

// Spacing: gaps, paddings and margins.
@ZigSpace1 = 4;
@ZigSpace2 = 8;
@ZigSpace3 = 12;
@ZigSpace4 = 16;
@ZigSpace5 = 24;
@ZigSpace6 = 32;

// Heights. A list row's three are its least, with a one-line title (its #RowStrut): a title on two lines grows the
// row.
@ZigRowHeight = 56;
@ZigCompactRowHeight = 44;
@ZigTallRowHeight = 74;
@ZigSectionHeadHeight = 32;
@ZigLineHeight = 32;
@ZigControlHeight = 32;
@ZigActionHeight = 40;
@ZigHeaderHeight = 60;
@ZigPillHeight = 24;

// Picture rungs. 64 is an item icon's own size, so no picture draws one larger.
@ZigPicInline = 20;
@ZigPicLine = 28;
@ZigPicRow = 32;
@ZigPicTile = 40;
@ZigPicHeader = 48;
@ZigPicLarge = 64;
